0156,"seed":604032295710653252,"stop":"eos","text":"Since \\( 12! = 479001600 \\), we know \\( a = 9 \\).\n\nTo verify \\( a = 9 \\) using the divisibility rule for 9, we sum the digits of the number \\( 479001600 \\):\n\\[\n4 + 7 + 9 + 0 + 0 + 1 + 6 + 0 + 0 = 27\n\\]\nSince 27 is divisible by 9, the digit \\( a \\) is indeed 9.\n\nThus, the value of \\( a \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"Since \\( 12! = 479001600 \\), we know \\( a = 9 \\).\n\nTo verify \\( a = 9 \\) using the divisibility rule for 9, we sum the digits of the number \\( 479001600 \\):\n\\[\n4 + 7 + 9 + 0 + 0 + 1 + 6 + 0 + 0 = 27\n\\]\nSince 27 is divisible by 9, the digit \\( a \\) is indeed 9.\n\nThus, the value of \\( a \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).","id":"number_theory:51"}
